From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] setup.py: force platlib placement for auditwheel

custom_bdist_wheel.finalize_options sets root_is_pure = False to get a
platform-specific wheel tag, but setup.py declares no ext_modules, so
distutils' install_lib command still treats the build as pure and
installs every file (including librnnoise.so) under the wheel's
purelib data category. auditwheel's manylinux/musllinux repair step
refuses to process a shared library placed there: "Invalid binary
wheel, found the following shared library/libraries in purelib
folder: librnnoise.so. The wheel has to be platlib compliant in order
to be repaired by auditwheel."

Overriding has_ext_modules() to True makes install_lib install the
whole package to platlib instead, which lands it at the wheel root
with no .data split and lets auditwheel repair the wheel normally.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [upstream's own release.yml never runs auditwheel on any platform, so this only matters for a build pipeline like this one's]
---
 setup.py | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/setup.py b/setup.py
index a6fba1b..ca22400 100644
--- a/setup.py
+++ b/setup.py
@@ -23,6 +23,7 @@ class custom_bdist_wheel(bdist_wheel):
     def finalize_options(self):
         bdist_wheel.finalize_options(self)
         self.root_is_pure = False
+        self.distribution.has_ext_modules = lambda: True

     def get_tag(self):
         python, abi, plat = bdist_wheel.get_tag(self)
--
